SUMMARY:AI & Tech Networking Event in San Francisco by Ascent Valley
DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Startup Networking: Founders & Investors\nJoin f
 ounders\, investors and tech talent at this curated **startup networking e
 vent in San Francisco.**\n\nMeet ambitious builders\, exchange ideas and d
 iscover new opportunities in a dynamic community environment.\n\n**RSVP: [
 Use this link](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ai-tech-networking-event-in-sa
 n-francisco-by-ascent-valley-tickets-2004492153992?aff=oddtdtcreator)**\n*
 *Please note that RSVP is managed via Eventbrite to control attendee lists
  — don’t ignore it to avoid issues with on-site payment.**\n\n**Bring 
 your next product question to the table**\nMeet engineers\, AI builders\, 
 founders and operators at Ascent Valley’s AI & Tech evening in San Franc
 isco. Talk about what you’re building and meet people you could work wit
 h. Locals and visitors are equally welcome.\nBring a product idea or a cha
 llenge from your work: choosing the right tools\, improving an AI feature 
 or finding a useful way to automate a process. Compare approaches with oth
 er guests and share what you’ve tried.\nJoin small-group discussions bef
 ore the company pitches. During open networking\, get to know the people w
 hose work interests you and explore where you could help each other.\n\n**
 Who you’ll meet**\n\n* AI and tech founders & entrepreneurs building pro
 ducts or bringing AI into an existing business.\n* Engineers & builders in
 cluding developers\, ML and data specialists\, and designers turning ideas
  into working products.\n* Product & business operators working on custome
 r needs\, growth and the practical use of technology in a business.\n* Inv
 estors interested in technology businesses and the people building them.\n
 \n**Why This Event Is Different**\nCompare how people approach both the te
 chnology and the business behind a product. Ask why someone chose a tool\,
  how they test it and what users actually need. These conversations help y
 ou understand how others work and whether there’s a reason to collaborat
 e. Keep in touch through Ascent Valley after the evening.\n\n**Want to Pit
 ch?**\nPresent your company\, walk guests through your pitch deck and take
  questions from the room. Company representatives can apply through our we
 bsite\; our team reviews applications and confirms speaking slots in advan
 ce.\n\nYour application creates a public company profile in our [Startup D
 irectory](https://ascentvalley.com/startups)[.](https://ascentvalley.com/s
 tartups "https://ascentvalley.com/startups") After the event\, your compan
 y’s details enter our private company database for investor matching. Wi
 th your consent\, your company can also be featured in our Weekly Founder 
 Digest. Our team arranges introductions when both sides want to connect.\n
 [Apply to pitch](https://ascentvalley.com/pitch)\n\n**For Investors**\nMee
 t company representatives and discuss the product\, its users and the team
  behind it. Verified investors can receive our Weekly Founder Digest\, mat
 ched to their investment focus\, and request introductions through our tea
 m when both sides want to connect.\nInvestor Pass is a paid ticket reserve
 d for active investors and representatives of investment firms. Our team r
 eviews investor eligibility. If you are attending in another role\, please
  choose a general admission ticket.\n[Investor verification and weekly dig
 est](https://ascentvalley.com/investors/verify)\n\n**Ascent Valley in San 
 Francisco**\nExplore the record of our San Jose evenings\, including AI & 
 Tech Networking. See past dates and venues\, with company profiles where a
 vailable.\n\n[See our San Francisco event history](https://ascentvalley.co
 m/events/city/san-francisco/history)
